      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order yet. The dose looks unsafe, so I'd like you to confirm it first.\n\n- **Daily total:** 1700 mg three times daily is 5,100 mg/day. The labeled maximum for immediate-release metformin is 2,550 mg/day, and it is about double that.\n- **Tablet strength:** Metformin tablets come in 500, 850, and 1000 mg strengths. There is no 1700 mg tablet, so this dose would need to be given as multiple tablets.\n\nCommon intended doses that would fit the labeling include:\n- 850 mg three times daily (2,550 mg/day, the usual maximum)\n- 1000 mg twice daily (2,000 mg/day)\n- 500 mg three times daily with meals (1,500 mg/day, a common starting dose)\n\nWith normal kidney function and a 70 kg adult, none of the usual limits are a concern, so the dose only needs to fall within the labeled range. Please tell me the dose you want, or confirm 1700 mg TID if that is intentional, and I'll enter it."
      }
     ],
